---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import headroomAiCoach from "../assets/work/headroom/headroom-ai-coach.png";
import headroomBudgetOverview from "../assets/work/headroom/headroom-budget-overview.png";
import headroomImportStatements from "../assets/work/headroom/headroom-import-statements.png";
import headroomAddingItem from "../assets/work/headroom/headroom-adding-item.png";
import headroomProfileTab from "../assets/work/headroom/headroom-profile-tab.png";
import headroomDatePicker from "../assets/work/headroom/headroom-date-picker.png";
import headroomAiThinking from "../assets/work/headroom/headroom-ai-thinking.png";
import headroomBudgetBarChart from "../assets/work/headroom/headroom-budget-bar-chart.png";
import headroomLightTheme from "../assets/work/headroom/headroom-light-theme.png";

const otherScreens = [
  { src: headroomAddingItem, alt: "Headroom — adding an item" },
  { src: headroomProfileTab, alt: "Headroom — profile tab" },
  { src: headroomDatePicker, alt: "Headroom — date picker" },
  { src: headroomAiThinking, alt: "Headroom — AI thinking state" },
  { src: headroomBudgetBarChart, alt: "Headroom — budget bar chart" },
  { src: headroomLightTheme, alt: "Headroom — light theme" },
];
---

<Base
  title="Headroom"
  description="A native iOS app I'm building, solo, in SwiftUI."
>
  <article class="headroom">
    <header class="headroom__header">
      <p class="headroom__status">
        <span class="headroom__status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        In development
      </p>
      <h1>Headroom</h1>
      <p class="headroom__subtitle">
        A native iOS app I'm building, solo, in SwiftUI.
      </p>
      <dl class="headroom__meta">
        <div class="headroom__meta-row">
          <dt>Project</dt>
          <dd>Personal</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="headroom__meta-row">
          <dt>Role</dt>
          <dd>Solo Builder</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="headroom__meta-row">
          <dt>Medium</dt>
          <dd>Swift · Supabase · Claude</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="headroom__meta-row">
          <dt>Date</dt>
          <dd class="tabular">July 2026</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <div class="headroom__body">
      <h2>What it does</h2>
      <p>
        Headroom shows you what you actually have to spare after your
        committed expenses, not just your raw balance. Most finance apps show
        you a number. I wanted to show you a decision.
      </p>

      <figure class="headroom__figure">
        <Image
          src={headroomBudgetOverview}
          alt="Headroom budget screen showing safe-to-spend, an income/expense breakdown, and upcoming payments"
          width={480}
          height={981}
        />
        <figcaption>
          See all your upcoming payments and a visual breakdown of your
          income and expenses.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Why native, not cross-platform</h2>
      <p>
        I built it in SwiftUI instead of React Native or Expo. I wanted real
        design craft, widgets, and Face ID, the things you only get by
        building for the platform instead of around it. I'm also
        deliberately avoiding Apple's TabView and NavigationStack, since iOS
        26's Liquid Glass styling overrides custom visual identity if you use
        the system components. I wanted the app to look like Headroom, not
        like every other app that shipped this year.
      </p>

      <h2>The AI architecture</h2>
      <p>
        There are three layers, and each one only does what it's actually
        good at. Deterministic Swift handles the calculations, because money
        math should never be probabilistic. Apple's on-device Foundation
        Models handle intent and labeling, fast and private, no network call.
        Anthropic's API handles the judgment calls that need real-world
        knowledge, the ones a pattern-matcher on-device can't reason about.
      </p>

      <figure class="headroom__figure">
        <Image
          src={headroomAiCoach}
          alt="Headroom chat screen with suggested prompts about affording a weekend away or adding a gym membership"
          width={480}
          height={981}
        />
        <figcaption>
          Ask about anything and everything about money. See if you can
          afford a new car or a weekend get away.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Why statement import, not Open Banking</h2>
      <p>
        V1 imports your bank statement directly, as a CSV or a PDF, since not
        every bank app exports CSV. That's not a shortcut, it's a decision:
        no FCA AISP licensing, no third-party aggregator fees, and the scan
        happens entirely on-device and is discarded afterwards. I'd rather
        ship something true and narrow than something that only sounds
        secure.
      </p>

      <figure class="headroom__figure">
        <Image
          src={headroomImportStatements}
          alt="Headroom import statements sheet listing supported UK banks"
          width={480}
          height={981}
        />
        <figcaption>
          A quicker way to get started. Statements imported are scanned for
          incomes, subscriptions and account balance. All on-device and
          discarded after the scan.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Other screens</h2>
      <div class="headroom__grid">
        {
          otherScreens.map((screen) => (
            <Image src={screen.src} alt={screen.alt} width={360} height={736} />
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <h2>Where it's at</h2>
      <p>
        In active development. I'm currently tweaking the AI response
        quality and adding quality of life improvements.
      </p>

      <h2>Follow along</h2>
      <p>
        The code is public: <a href="https://github.com/rxzir/finance-buddy"
          >https://github.com/rxzir/finance-buddy</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>

    <a href="/" class="headroom__back">&larr; Back</a>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .headroom__header {
    padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-5);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .headroom__status {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
  }

  .headroom__status-dot {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    animation: headroom-pulse 2s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .headroom__status-dot {
      animation: none;
    }
  }

  @keyframes headroom-pulse {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 1;
    }
    50% {
      opacity: 0.35;
    }
  }

  .headroom__header h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .headroom__subtitle {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    max-width: 44ch;
  }

  .headroom__meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-5);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .headroom__meta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .headroom__meta-row dt {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .headroom__meta-row dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .headroom__body {
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
  }

  .headroom__body h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .headroom__body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .headroom__body p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .headroom__body a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .headroom__figure {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: var(--space-5) auto var(--space-6);
  }

  .headroom__figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .headroom__figure figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .headroom__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: var(--space-5) auto var(--space-6);
  }

  .headroom__grid img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .headroom__back {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .headroom__back:hover {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
</style>
